&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PORTLAND, Ore.&ndash;&lt;/strong&gt; The VA Portland Health Care System's Lincoln City Community Based Outpatient Clinic (CBOC) is set to close on Tuesday, March 31.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Veterans are being transitioned to other VA clinics or community providers. If Veterans and caregivers have any questions or concerns, they are encouraged to call the VA Portland Patient Aligned Care Team (PACT) at 971-304-2200, ext. 2, or send a message through MyHealth&lt;em&gt;e&lt;/em&gt;Vet.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Newport VA Clinic will remain open for lab services for Veterans who were previously assigned to Lincoln City or Newport. Care teams will continue to manage Veterans&rsquo; care virtually after March 31, 2026, until patients are established with new providers.&lt;/p&gt;

