&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Sisters of St. Mary of Oregon&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style="color:rgb(102, 102, 102); font-size:10pt"&gt;Founded in 1886, the Sisters of St. Mary of Oregon live as women of prayer in simplicity and sisterly love who are called to be compassionate, joyful servants of the Lord. There are currently 40 Sisters in the SSMO Community, most of whom live in the historic domed Motherhouse in Beaverton, Oregon. The Sisters' sponsored ministries include Valley Catholic School, Maryville Care Center, the Sisters of St. Mary of Oregon Foundation, and Sisters of St. Mary of Oregon Ministries Corporation. Approximately 550 people partner with the Sisters serving more than 1000 children and 140 Maryville residents and supporting dozens of ministries throughout the Pacific Northwest. To learn more about visiting or joining the Sisters of St. Mary of Oregon, visit &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="http://ssmo.org" style="text-decoration-line: none;"&gt;&lt;span style="color:rgb(17, 85, 204); font-size:10pt"&gt;ssmo.org&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:rgb(102, 102, 102); font-size:10pt"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

